    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d744">

                <pb facs="0912" n="830" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg830"/>

                <head>Mr. Motley to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 150.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Vienna</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 27, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I think it is well to state, referring to
                    my confidential despatch No.148, of date February 20, 1866, that I have been
                    informed that efforts are making to induce the Austrian government to consent
                    that 4,000 volunteers may be levied here this year for Mexico, on the ground
                    that the supplementary article to the convention of Miramar permitted two
                    thousand each year, and that none were forwarded in the year 1865.</p>
                <p>I learn that this consent will probably be accorded, so that if the funds can be
                    obtained for paying, equipping, and transporting them, 4,000 Austrian volunteers
                    will be found and may be expected in Mexico this year. I believe that the funds
                    have not yet been furnished.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to remain your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. LOTHROP MOTLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
